        name = "Red Flying Cloud",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=89363",
        tips = "",
        mountCategory = "Vendor",
        stepCount = 10,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - A deterministic sightseeing route and story hand-ins; flight makes it much faster.\n\n1. Start with Lorewalker Cho at the Seat of Knowledge above Mogu'shan Palace (Vale 83.2,29.6) and complete Your Private Collection if offered. Fly the Jade Forest route: Saurok, Watersmithing, Hozen Speech, Xin Wu Yin, Spirit Binders, Emperor's Burden 1 and 3, and The First Monks. Click/read each object; flying past gives no credit.\n\n2. In the Valley of the Four Winds read A Most Famous Bill of Sale, The Birthplace of Liu Lang, Wandering Widow, Waterspeakers, Embracing the Passion and Pandaren Fighting Tactics. The pins share this step number because they form one zone leg.\n\n3. In Krasarang Wilds read Waiting for the Turtle, Last Stand, Origins, Hozen Maturity, Quan Tou Kuo, The Lost Dynasty and Emperor's Burden 4. Hozen Maturity is on the far southern island.\n\n4. Visit the Veiled Stair and read The Defiant inside the Ancient Passage. Use the separate Veiled Stair map choice rather than treating this object as a Kun-Lai surface pin.\n\n5. In Kun-Lai Summit read Role Call, The Hozen Ravage, Ren Yun the Blind, Valley of Emperors, Emperor's Burdens 2, 6 and 7, Yaungol, Yaungol Tactics and Victory in Kun-Lai. Valley of Emperors is inside the tomb; enter from the valley and follow the passage.\n\n6. In Townlong Steppes read Emperor's Burden 5, Dominance and Trapped in a Strange Land.\n\n7. In the Dread Wastes read The Deserters, Amber, Cycle of the Mantid, Mantid Society and The Empress.\n\n8. In the earlier Vale of Eternal Blossoms read The Thunder King, Emperor's Burden 8, Always Remember and Together, We Are Strong. Use Zidormi near 81.2,29.6 if the Black Empire assault phase hides the earlier objects.\n\n9. When a lore collection achievement completes, check your mailbox for its quest scroll. Use the scroll, return to Cho at the Seat of Knowledge, hand it in and let his story finish. Complete additional collections/story turn-ins until Exalted; use the Grand Commendation at Revered to increase remaining gains.\n\n10. Buy Disc of the Red Flying Cloud from Tan Shin Tiao at 82.2,29.4 beside Cho and use it. If your reputation is short, check which objects or mailed story quests remain unfinished instead of repeating already-read objects.",
    },
